  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 11,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/1f0481bb8e1e2b54a0a03bf2a8747935e6313be4/docs%2Fserving%2Fonline_serving%2Fopenai_compatible_server.md",
      "changes": 11,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/docs%2Fserving%2Fonline_serving%2Fopenai_compatible_server.md?ref=1f0481bb8e1e2b54a0a03bf2a8747935e6313be4",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/serving/online_serving/openai_compatible_server.md",
      "patch": "@@ -229,3 +229,14 @@ The following extra parameters in the response object are supported:\n     ```python\n     --8<-- \"vllm/entrypoints/openai/responses/protocol.py:responses-response-extra-params\"\n     ```\n+\n+\n+## Streaming Cancellation and Resource Reclamation\n+\n+When serving online inference with streaming generation via Server-Sent Events (SSE), client connections may be terminated unexpectedly (such as user navigation or network drops).\n+\n+vLLM `AsyncLLMEngine` listens for client disconnect events and triggers request cancellation:\n+\n+* The active sequence is removed from the running scheduling queues.\n+* Allocated KV cache blocks are promptly released back to `BlockManager` to avoid GPU memory leaks.\n+* In-flight generation for the cancelled request is aborted to conserve compute resources.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/1f0481bb8e1e2b54a0a03bf2a8747935e6313be4/docs%2Fserving%2Fonline_serving%2Fopenai_compatible_server.md",
      "sha": "da4649ad31c89249125106b3159fc1b08e72e1a7",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
